Anchored tabs: most-recently-active visibility in collapsed groups, a fix
for closing the active tab, and forcing new tabs to the bottom section.

- When a tab group is collapsed, keep visible the tabs that are among the
  browser-wide 5 most-recently-active tabs (by last-active time) instead of only
  the active tab; tabs outside that set are hidden and hibernated off the
  current call stack. Adds helium::GetTopRecentlyActiveContents and
  helium::HibernateGroupTabsOutsideTopRecent.
- Removes the anchored-tabs fallback that force-added a replacement tab from
  inside TabStripModel::CloseTabs when the active tab was closed with no live
  fallback. That ran inside the close reentrancy guard (crashing on AddTab) and
  caused new tabs to "reopen instead of close". Closing now follows the standard
  path and activates the adjacent tab.
- Forces a brand-new tab (Cmd/Ctrl+T, the new-tab button, omnibox Alt+Enter) to
  open ungrouped at the bottom of the strip (the lower, non-anchored section) so
  it is never absorbed into the active tab's group.

